# Frontend Folder Structure

## Feature folder layout (under `src/app/(dashboard)/`)

Every feature follows this structure:

```
feature-name/
├── _api/                  # Raw API call functions (no hooks, no React)
│   └── feature.api.ts
├── _queries/              # React Query read hooks (useQuery)
│   └── feature.queries.ts
├── _mutations/            # React Query write hooks (useMutation)
│   └── feature.mutations.ts
├── _types/                # TypeScript types and interfaces
│   └── feature.types.ts
├── _components/           # UI components (one per file, no merging)
│   ├── feature-header.tsx
│   ├── feature-table.tsx
│   └── feature-detail.tsx
├── _utils/                # Pure helper functions (formatters, parsers)
│   └── format.ts
├── [id]/                  # Dynamic route for detail pages
│   ├── page.tsx
│   └── _components/       # Detail-specific components
├── page.tsx               # Main list/landing page
└── layout.tsx             # Optional layout wrapper
```

Example Zentron features that will follow this pattern:
`briefs/`, `creators/`, `campaigns/`, `contracts/`, `escrow/`, `score/`, `disputes/`.

## What goes where

### `_api/` — Raw API functions
- Plain async functions that call `api.get()`, `api.post()`, etc.
- No React hooks, no `useQuery`, no `useMutation`
- Returns typed responses
- Example: `fetchBriefList(params)`, `createBrief(payload)`

### `_queries/` — Read hooks
- Only `useQuery` hooks
- Import from `_api/` for the actual fetch functions
- Handle query keys, enabled flags, placeholderData
- Example: `useBriefList(filters)`, `useBriefDetail(id)`

### `_mutations/` — Write hooks
- Only `useMutation` hooks
- Import from `_api/` for the actual mutation functions
- Handle cache invalidation via `queryClient.invalidateQueries`
- Example: `useCreateBrief()`, `useUpdateBrief(id)`

### `_types/` — TypeScript types
- Entity types matching backend response shape
- Filter/query parameter types
- List response types with pagination
- No runtime code, only type definitions

### `_components/` — UI components
- One component per file, always
- Never merge multiple components into a single file
- Name files with the feature prefix: `brief-table.tsx`, not `table.tsx`
- Local sub-components go in sub-folders: `_components/detail/`

### `_utils/` — Pure helpers
- Formatters: `formatDate`, `formatAmount`, `formatScoreBand`
- Parsers, validators, mapping functions
- No React, no hooks, no side effects

## Global shared code

```
src/
├── components/
│   ├── ui/                # shadcn primitives (Input, Button, Dialog, Switch, etc.)
│   ├── forms/             # Form helpers (FormField, FormSelect, SectionHeader, CountrySelect)
│   ├── layout/            # App shell (sidebar, topbar)
│   └── marketing/         # Public landing-page sections
├── lib/
│   ├── api.ts             # Axios instance
│   ├── utils.ts           # cn() helper
│   ├── types.ts           # Shared types (onboarding, auth, roles)
│   └── permissions.ts     # Permission constants
├── hooks/                 # Cross-feature React hooks (use-*.ts)
├── providers/             # Context providers (ACL, React Query, Google OAuth)
├── store/                 # Redux Toolkit store, root reducer, typed hooks
├── types/                 # Globally shared types
└── middleware.ts          # Route gating (auth, onboarding, redirects)
```

## Rules

- Use shadcn `Input` and `Button` from `ui/` — never create parallel input/button components
- Use `FormSelect` from `forms/` for native `<select>` with react-hook-form `register()`
- Use shadcn `Dialog`, `Switch`, `Tabs` from `ui/` for complex interactions
- Shared hooks that multiple features use go in `src/app/(dashboard)/_hooks/`
- Never hardcode data that should come from an API (creators, niches, currencies, score weights)
- Every `useMutation` must have `onError` handling
- Destructive actions (delete, deactivate, cancel campaign) require confirmation before executing
